---
title: "Session host: one channel across dcserver restarts, host loss and terminate"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Recovery
    lg1: Session
    lg2: Path to the HostRecovers bug
    lg3: Repeats forever, so HostRecovers breaks
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 teal
  class lg2 bugPath
  class lg3 repeats
  s0: No session
  s1: No session, a message waiting
  s2: dcserver down, nothing running, a message waiting
  s3: Boot reconcile, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s4: No session, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s5: Creating, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s6: Created, location not yet recorded, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s7: Pane recorded, only a shell, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s8: Pane recorded, pane gone, host server down, a message waiting (after the restart)
  s9: Pane recorded, pane gone, host server down (after the restart)
  s10: Pane recorded, pane gone, host server down (after the restart) (no more messages)
  s11: No session, host server down (after the restart) (no more messages)
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: a message arrives
  s1 --> s1: a host probe stops failing
  s1 --> s2: dcserver stops
  s2 --> s3: dcserver starts
  s3 --> s4: intake opens
  s4 --> s5: a message reserves a new execution
  s5 --> s6: the host creates it
  s6 --> s7: its pane is recorded
  s7 --> s8: the host server ends
  s8 --> s9: the turn is refused: no provider in the pane
  s9 --> s8: a message arrives
  s8 --> s10: the turn is refused: no provider in the pane
  s10 --> s11: the recorded pane is gone: row closed
